/*
 * Hartwick Atelier — THE CIRCLE
 *
 * Aloha, 4 September 2026: "please add The Circle as a public page at
 * /the-circle and include it in the main navigation. The Circle and The
 * Register should remain separate."
 *
 * ⚠️ TWO THINGS THIS FILE CANNOT DO ON ITS OWN — both are Shopify Admin, not
 *    theme code, and both are listed in the handover note:
 *
 *      1. THE PAGE ITSELF. A theme can hold a page template; it cannot create
 *         the page record. Someone with Admin access must add a page titled
 *         "The Circle" (handle: the-circle) and set its Theme template to
 *         "the-circle". Until then this file is inert.
 *
 *      2. THE URL. Shopify serves pages at /pages/<handle> and does not allow
 *         a page at the site root. /the-circle therefore needs a URL redirect
 *         (Admin > Content > Menus > URL redirects) from /the-circle to
 *         /pages/the-circle. The redirect is the only way to honour the
 *         address Aloha asked for.
 *
 *      3. THE NAVIGATION. Menus live in Admin > Content > Menus, not in the
 *         theme. "The Circle" has to be added to the main menu there.
 *
 * ⚠️ TERMINOLOGY. Framework v3 — the top of the source-of-truth hierarchy —
 *    records The Circle as invitation-only, with no public form and no
 *    application route. This page is the opposite of that, and exists on
 *    Aloha's written instruction. The conflict is flagged for Christina.
 *    sections/ha-circle-request.liquid carries the detail and a single switch
 *    that removes the application route without touching the page.
 *
 * ⚠️ ALL COPY IS PROVISIONAL. The headings are transcribed from Aloha's own
 *    design; every body paragraph is an explicit placeholder, because nothing
 *    about what The Circle offers, how someone is considered, or what a member
 *    receives may be written by the build (CLAUDE.md, Content rules). Every
 *    section shows its provisional notice on screen.
 *
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * NOTE: this file is also written by the Shopify theme editor.
 *
 * GOTCHA, learned the hard way on 4 September 2026: Shopify validates a JSON
 * template against each section's schema AS IT EXISTS ON THE THEME at the
 * moment the template is uploaded, and silently drops any setting the schema
 * does not yet declare. So if you add a setting to a section AND set it here in
 * the same change, upload order decides whether it survives — and the CLI skips
 * files whose contents have not changed, so `touch` will not re-send it. If a
 * setting here mysteriously reads as its schema default, edit this file for
 * real (a byte is enough) so it is re-uploaded after the section.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 */
